  "claims": [
    "A bounded exact-out allocation domain can be represented as finite feasible and emitted sets, with emitted-key equality following from pointwise generator completeness.",
    "Every feasible allocation has a sorted, duplicate-free support presentation whose leg amounts sum to the target.",
    "For a nonempty feasible domain, selected-domain canonical existence follows from the exact-out canonical minimizer.",
    "For a feasible support presentation with a head leg and residual tail, the head amount lies within concrete capacity and remaining-target bounds.",
    "Residual allocation erases the selected head support and preserves the tail support presentation needed for recursion.",
    "Reindexed residual allocation preserves support sets, support indices, support legs, and feasibility under a residual target.",
    "The remaining-capacity envelope and top-sum bounds are sufficient to justify concrete recursion ranges.",
    "A feasible support presentation is structurally reachable by the selected-domain recursion, and concrete recursion reduction packages the exact induction step."
  ],
  "proof_method": [
    "finite-set image and equality reasoning for emitted and feasible domains",
    "support-set sorting and sum preservation over finite allocations",
    "residual-allocation construction by erasing the head support",
    "reindexing lemmas to move residual targets through the same support presentation",
    "remaining-capacity envelope/top-sum inequalities for range safety",
    "structural induction over sorted support presentations"
  ],
